<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      strategy_defaults row for Strategy 5 (Pressure).

      WHY target_mode / sl_mode = POINTS
      ==================================
      The Pressure spec's bracket is an absolute +50 / -50 on the option premium,
      identical for every leg it trades. The default for a strategy with no row
      here is PERCENT (BracketMode.parse(null)), which would resolve the bracket
      as a FRACTION of entry premium and silently give an ITM300 leg trading at
      ~350 a 70-point target instead of a 50-point one. That is a 40% wider
      bracket than specified, on every trade, and nothing would log it.

      This is precisely the S6 inertness class of bug the 041 changeset
      documents, arriving from the other direction: there the columns existed
      and were not read, here the row would not exist and the default would be
      wrong for this strategy.

      WHY auto_config_enabled = FALSE
      ===============================
      This is the load-bearing part for "do not change the existing strategies".

      EodDowntrendDetectionService walks every sma_downtrend_rule at end of day
      and generates next-day trade_config rows for each strategy tagged on it.
      Strategy 5 must never appear in that output: its configs are a measurement
      book with a fixed clock, an exact strike offset and a book id, and the
      detector knows about none of those - it would emit half-configured rows
      that run as an unbounded-clock, depth-count strategy. Worse, they would
      interleave with strategies 1-4's generated configs on the same dates.

      Pressure configs come from PressureConfigGenerator instead, which is an
      explicit, dated, idempotent bulk operation. FALSE here is what keeps the
      two lineages apart, and the detector logs by name when it skips a
      disabled strategy rather than doing it silently.

      WHY lot_quantity / max_loss / no_of_trades ARE PLACEHOLDERS
      ==========================================================
      Every column on this table exists for the DETECTOR to stamp onto configs
      it generates. With auto_config_enabled = FALSE nothing here is ever
      copied anywhere - PressureConfigGenerator sets each of these on the
      config rows itself, from the spec. They are filled with the table's
      NOT NULL requirements satisfied and nothing more; the two that DO get
      read at order time, whatever generated the config, are target_mode and
      sl_mode above.
    -->
    <changeSet id="044_seed_pressure_strategy_defaults" author="moneymaker">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM strategy_defaults WHERE strategy_id = 5
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <insert tableName="strategy_defaults">
            <column name="strategy_id" valueNumeric="5"/>
            <!--
              Nominal only. Pressure runs BOTH directions across its books
              (SELL_* and BUY_*), and the direction that actually gates an entry
              is trade_config.transaction_type on each individual config, which
              OrderService reads. This column is only ever consumed by the
              detector, which is disabled below.
            -->
            <column name="transaction_type" value="SELL"/>
            <column name="lot_quantity" valueNumeric="75"/>
            <column name="max_loss" valueNumeric="0"/>
            <column name="no_of_trades" valueNumeric="0"/>
            <column name="no_of_parallel_trades" valueNumeric="1"/>
            <!-- See the header: this is what keeps Pressure out of the EOD detector. -->
            <column name="auto_config_enabled" valueBoolean="false"/>
            <column name="opposite_side" valueBoolean="false"/>
            <!-- The two that matter. See the header. -->
            <column name="target_mode" value="POINTS"/>
            <column name="sl_mode" value="POINTS"/>
        </insert>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
